bench: reports differ in `config`: {"sheet":"empty","script":"pan","frames":600,"warmup":60,"window_logical":[1536.0,864.0],"scene_counts":false} vs {"sheet":"empty","script":"pan","frames":600,"warmup":60,"window_logical":[1536.0,864.0],"scene_counts":false,"diagnostic_trace":true}

usage: bench <command> [options]

  run     [--sheet empty|t01|placeholder] [--script pan|zoom] [--frames 600] [--warmup 60]
          [--size 1280x800] [--json FILE]
  spike   s1..s6|s8 [--count N] [--mode fixed|sweep|square|rounded|sprite|direct|direct-sweep|cached|repaint|quality|monitors|displays]
          [--frames 600] [--warmup 60] [--size 3072x1728] [--json FILE]
  start   [--sheet empty|t01|placeholder] [--runs 10] [--size 960x640] [--json FILE]
  idle    [--sheet empty|t01|placeholder] [--seconds 10] [--settle-ms 1000] [--size 960x640] [--json FILE]
  hit     [--sheet 10k|1k|100|dense|text] [--samples 20000] [--seed 42] [--json FILE]
  compare BASE.json NEW.json [--max-regression 10] [--metrics PREFIX[,PREFIX..]]
          [--json FILE]
  spike   s7 [--seconds 60] [--out FILE] | s7 --summarise FILE

Every command exits by itself. Exit codes: 0 ok; 1 compare found a regression or a missing
metric; 2 usage or input error, including reports that cannot be compared or a --metrics
prefix that selects no base metric; 3 the run failed or timed out. compare --json writes
the per-metric result and the verdict whether it passes or finds a regression.
